## Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js App Router project.

### Changes Made:

**Modified Files:**
1. `landing/app/layout.js` - Added Analytics component
   - Imported `Analytics` from `@vercel/analytics/next`
   - Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag, following the official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router

2. `landing/package.json` - Added dependency
   - Added `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 to dependencies

3. `landing/package-lock.json` - Updated lock file
   - Updated with the new @vercel/analytics package and its dependencies

### Implementation Details:

- **Framework Detection**: Identified Next.js App Router project (app/layout.js exists)
- **Package Manager**: Used npm (package-lock.json present)
- **Installation**: Ran `npm install @vercel/analytics` successfully
- **Configuration**: Followed official Vercel documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
- **Placement**: Analytics component placed at the end of the body tag for optimal page load performance

### Verification:

✓ Build completed successfully (`npm run build`)
✓ No new linting errors introduced (pre-existing linting issues remain in unrelated files)
✓ Analytics component properly imported and integrated
✓ Dependencies updated in package.json and package-lock.json

### How It Works:

Once deployed to Vercel, the Analytics component will automatically:
- Track page views and visitor data
- Send analytics data to your Vercel dashboard
- Provide real-time insights about website traffic

No additional configuration is required. Analytics will be enabled automatically on Vercel deployment.
